n to his brethren. — Ge 45:1-8.","refs":[["Gen",45,1,45,8]]},{"text":"Joseph sends for his father. — Ge 45:9-11.","refs":[["Gen",45,9,45,11]]},{"text":"Pharaoh invites Jacob into. — Ge 45:16-20.","refs":[["Gen",45,16,45,20]]},{"text":"Jacob’s journey. — Ge 46:5-7.","refs":[["Gen",46,5,46,7]]},{"text":"Jacob, &c presented to Pharaoh. — Ge 47:1-10.","refs":[["Gen",47,1,47,10]]},{"text":"Israel placed in the land of Goshen. — Ge 46:34; 47:11,27.","refs":[["Gen",46,34,46,34],["Gen",47,11,47,11],["Gen",47,27,47,27]]},{"text":"Joseph enriches the king. — Ge 47:13-26.","refs":[["Gen",47,13,47,26]]},{"text":"Jacob’s death and burial. — Ge 49:33; 50:1-13.","refs":[["Gen",49,33,49,33],["Gen",50,1,50,13]]},{"text":"Israel increases and are oppressed. — Ex 1:1-14.","refs":[["Exod",1,1,1,14]]},{"text":"Male children destroyed. — Ex 1:15-22.","refs":[["Exod",1,15,1,22]]},{"text":"Moses born and hid for three months. — Ex 2:2.","refs":[["Exod",2,2,2,2]]},{"text":"Moses exposed on the Nile. — Ex 2:3,4.","refs":[["Exod",2,3,2,3],["Exod",2,4,2,4]]},{"text":"Moses adopted and brought up by Pharaoh’s daughter. — Ex 2:5-10.","refs":[["Exod",2,5,2,10]]},{"text":"Moses slays an Egyptian. — Ex 2:11,12.","refs":[["Exod",2,11,2,11],["Exod",2,12,2,12]]},{"text":"Moses flies to Midian. — Ex 2:15.","refs":[["Exod",2,15,2,15]]},{"text":"Moses sent to Pharaoh. — Ex 3:2-10.","refs":[["Exod",3,2,3,10]]},{"text":"Pharaoh increases their affliction. — Ex 5:1-23.","refs":[["Exod",5,1,5,23]]},{"text":"Moses proves his divine mission by miracles. — Ex 4:29-31; 7:10.","refs":[["Exod",4,29,4,31],["Exod",7,10,7,10]]},{"text":"Egypt is plagued for Pharaoh’s obstinacy. — Ex 7:14-10:29.","refs":[["Exod",7,14,10,29]]},{"text":"The passover instituted. — Ex 12:1-28.","refs":[["Exod",12,1,12,28]]},{"text":"Destruction of the first-born. — Ex 12:29,30.","refs":[["Exod",12,29,12,29],["Exod",12,30,12,30]]},{"text":"Israel spoils the Egyptians. — Ex 12:35,36.","refs":[["Exod",12,35,12,35],["Exod",12,36,12,36]]},{"te